title: StartDay3
position: -125,-487
---
<<set $daysPassed = 681>>
<<play_sound AlarmClock>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
I wake to the alarm again. My body knows the routine now. The ache, the fog, the slow reassembly of self.
Cryosleep doesn't get easier. You just get better at pretending it does.
I blink at the mission clock.
Day {$daysPassed}.
Another two months dissolved into nothing. That's over four months from Earth now.
The ship smells the same. The silence sounds the same. But something in my chest has shifted.
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
I know there's someone out there. And they know I'm here. The thought still carries warmth, even after the ice.
<<else>>
I know there's someone out there. And they know I'm here.
<<endif>>
<<show_ui ClickToInteract>>
<<show MonitorOffDay3>>
===

title: OnClickedMonitorDay3
position: -128,-338
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I power on the monitor. The usual HQ digest loads. Mission parameters unchanged, supply inventory nominal, another reminder about reporting protocols.
But underneath the routine, the comms buffer has a new entry.
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
A single packet, tagged with {$catName}'s frequency. The translator renders it into a short burst.
<<speed 0.4>>
<<play_sound RobotTalk 0.25>>
"STILL HERE" <i>[12 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<speed 1>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
Two words, sent while I was frozen. A reminder that patience doesn't require a heartbeat.
Something in my chest loosens. They waited. Again.
<<else>>
Two words. Twelve days ago.
<<endif>>
I note the timestamp and close the buffer. I'll deal with that later. For now, the day needs a shape.
    -> (start the day)
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
===

title: RegularTasksDay3
position: 260,308
---
<<once>>
<<declare $day3DidPushups = false>>
<<declare $day3DidStargaze = false>>
<<declare $day3DidSystemsCheck = false>>
<<endonce>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
The ship hums beneath me. I have time before anything demands my attention.
My body is stiff from cryosleep. My mind is restless. I should do something with both.
    -> (do some push-ups) <<if $day3DidPushups == false>>
        <<set $day3DidPushups = true>>
        I drop to the floor. The count is slower today, my arms heavier, but the rhythm is still mine.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        By the end I'm breathing hard, but I feel more present in my own skin.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (stare at the stars) <<if $day3DidStargaze == false>>
        <<set $day3DidStargaze = true>>
        I press my face close to the viewport and let the stars fill my vision until there's no room for anything else.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        For a few minutes, the loneliness fades into something closer to wonder.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (check the ship systems) <<if $day3DidSystemsCheck == false>>
        <<set $day3DidSystemsCheck = true>>
        I pull up the diagnostics panel. Life support, comms, power draw. All within tolerance.
        One line catches my eye. Long-term oxygen reserves are slightly below projected baseline. Not critical. Not yet.
        I make a mental note and move on.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (move on)
        <<jump PrepareReportDay3>>
===

title: PrepareReportDay3
position: 259,417
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I sit down at the terminal. The report template blinks at me, the same empty fields I've filled a hundred times.
Before I can type the first word, the comms panel lights up.
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
<<show MonitorSilhouette>>
{$catName}'s frequency. Live this time, not a recording.
    -> (answer)
        <<jump CallCatDay3>>
    -> (ignore it and write the report first)
        I try to focus on the report. The cursor blinks. The frequency pulses.
        I last about thirty seconds.
        <<jump CallCatDay3>>
===

title: CallCatDay3
position: 422,282
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<hide MonitorOn>>
<<show MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show_character Cat Obscure right>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
I open the channel. Static, then motion. The silhouette leans in, sharper than before, like the translator is getting better at rendering it.
<<play_music CatTheme 0.5>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    {$catName}: You came back! I was worried the sleep box ate you.
    {$catName}: I practice more word while you gone. Listen: "It is good to see you."
    {$catName}: Did I say right?
        -> Perfect.
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
            {$catName}: I practice that one many time.
        -> Close enough.
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            {$catName}: I take it. Close is still closer than before.
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    {$catName}: Oh. You answer. I was not sure you would.
        -> Of course I answered.
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
            {$catName}: Okay. Good.
<<endif>>
<<jump CatConvoDay3>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3
position: 647,285
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: So...
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The line stays open but neither of us fills it. I can hear the faint hum of whatever's on {$catName}'s end. A distant vibration, like wind through something hollow.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
I notice {$catName} shifting on screen, like they want to say something but keep swallowing it.
Last time we couldn't stop talking. Now we can't seem to start.
    -> What are you thinking about?
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: I... okay. I want ask you something. If okay.
    -> You've gone quiet.
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: Yes. Sorry. I was trying to find right words.
        {$catName}: I want ask you something. If okay.
    -> ...
        {$catName}: Sorry for quiet. I was thinking...
{$catName}: When you sleep in box... do you dream?
    -> Sometimes. They feel more like memories.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: Memories that come when you not looking. I have those too.
        {$catName}: Mine are mostly sounds. My family talking over dinner. The hum of home.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        Sharing that feels unexpectedly easy.
    -> I'd rather not talk about it.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: Okay. I understand closed doors.
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        I shut down again. The habit is hard to break.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: I ask because... I been thinking about time. How it work different for us.
{$catName}: My people... we not live as long as humans. Much shorter. What is months for you is... big part of life for me.
{$catName}: Every day I wait for you to wake up, I feel it. The weight of it. Like sand running out that I cannot put back.
{$catName}: I count them. Every one.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: Sometimes I wonder if you forget me between sleeps. If I am just... noise you heard once.
{$catName}: You have so many year ahead. For me, the time we already spend... it is not small. It is real.
    -> I haven't forgotten you.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: That mean more than you know.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        Saying it out loud makes it feel true.
    -> We barely know each other.
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: ...Yes. You are right. But I hoped anyway.
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        The honesty was supposed to feel clean. Instead it tastes like rust.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The signal holds. {$catName} is still there, waiting.
    -> (keep talking)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_Part2>>
    -> (end the conversation)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_Part2
position: 647,400
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: Can I tell you something? About my planet?
{$catName}: I know last time I say I not allowed. And I still not. But...
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: My people, they have word for humans. Rough translation is... "loud silence." You fill space with noise but never say real thing.
{$catName}: They think you dangerous. Not because weapon. Because you lonely and you don't know it.
{$catName}: Lonely thing with power is... unpredictable.
    -> That's... not unfair.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: You surprise me. Most people not like hearing truth about themselves.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        Accepting it hurts, but it also feels honest.
    -> That's a pretty harsh generalization.
        <<negative_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: Maybe. But you sitting alone in metal box in space. You tell me I wrong?
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        I want to argue. I can't.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: My father... he most afraid of all. He very careful with me. Keep me close. Always.
{$catName}: He not mean. He love me. But his love feel like... wall? Like small room with no window.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: And my people... they watch. Always watch. If I do wrong thing, they know.
{$catName}: They have big rule. Because of what happen long time ago. When human come before.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: I grow up hearing that story. Everyone afraid because of it. Father most of all.
{$catName}: He say never talk to human. Never. Not even think about it.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: But I hear your ship. Your voice in the noise. And I think... this not sound like monster.
{$catName}: This sound like person. Alone person. Like me.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: You are first thing in my life nobody tell me to want.
{$catName}: First thing I choose. Just me. No rule. No father. No story.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: That why they not want me talk to you. They afraid you... infect me. With your loneliness.
{$catName}: But I think loneliness not disease. I think it just... wound that need air.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: I already have wound. Talking to you not make it worse. It make it... known.
    -> You're braver than I am.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: No. I just more desperate. Brave and desperate look same from outside.
    -> What happens if your people find out about us?
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: I... not want to think about that.
        {$catName}: For now, we careful. That has to be enough.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The weight of what {$catName} just shared settles between us like dust after an explosion.
    -> (keep talking)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_Part3>>
    -> (end the conversation)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_Part3
position: 647,515
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: Enough heavy talk. I want ask lighter thing.
<<if $catLikesYou <= $catDislikesYou>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The pivot feels deliberate. 
Like {$catName} is scanning through a mental list of conversation topics, looking for one that will land. 
I recognize the move. I've done it myself... reaching for lightness when the connection isn't carrying itself anymore.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<endif>>
{$catName}: What is thing you miss most? From your planet?
    -> Rain.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: Rain? Water falling from sky?
        {$catName}: We have something like that. But ours is warm. And it hum.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: I miss the humming rain. Maybe I play recording for you sometime.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        The idea of sharing something so small and specific makes the distance feel a little shorter.
    -> Nothing.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: ...Nothing? Not one thing?
        {$catName}: That make me sad for you.
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        I said it to sound tough. It just sounds empty.
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
    {$catName}: I want show you something. Hold on.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    The screen flickers. For a brief moment, the silhouette shifts and I catch a glimpse of something behind {$catName}: a window, with an amber sky and shapes that might be trees, or might be something I have no word for.
    It lasts two seconds. Then the feed stabilizes back to the usual framing.
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    {$catName}: That was my sky. I wanted you to see it. Even just little bit.
        -> It's beautiful.
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
            {$catName}: It is. And now you carry piece of it.
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            Something about that gesture makes me feel less far from everything.
        -> Be careful! You don't want to get in trouble.
            <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
            {$catName}: ...You right. I was careless.
            <<negative_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            I said the practical thing. It doesn't feel like the right thing.
<<endif>>
<<jump CatConvoDay3_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_End
position: 647,630
---
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
The conversation settles into a comfortable lull. Neither of us seems to want to hang up. But it feels different from last time.
<<else>>
The conversation thins out. Neither of us hangs up, but neither of us reaches for the next thing to say either.
<<endif>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: I want tell you something. I been thinking about it since we first talk.
{$catName}: Long time ago, before I born, someone come to our planet. From very far away.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: My elders tell story about him. He was... strange. Tall. Clumsy. Always knocking things over because gravity different for him.
{$catName}: But he learn fast. He try to speak our language, even though his mouth not made for it. He sound terrible. Everyone laugh, but... kind laugh. Warm.
    -> Sounds like a character.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: Yes! He was. Very much.
    -> Where did he come from?
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: From far. A small blue planet. I think you know which one.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: He had this thing he carry everywhere. Small object, fit in hand. He say it was gift from his father. Had little... what is word... engraving? Of a bird.
{$catName}: He would hold it when he miss home. My elders say he rub the edges smooth over time.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
My breath catches. I know that object. A brass compass with a sparrow etched into the lid. It sat on my father's desk my entire childhood. He said his father gave it to him before he died.
He never said where it had been.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: He stay long time. Many season. My people, they... accept him. He was different, yes, but he try. He care.
{$catName}: He learn to cook our food. He fix things. He sit with the elders and listen to old stories, even when he not understand all words.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: They give him a name in our language. It mean "the one who listens with his whole body."
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: But then... he meet someone there. One of us. She was... important to many people. A healer. Everyone trust her.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: And one day, he take her and leave. Back to his planet. No warning. No goodbye to the rest.
{$catName}: She not want to go. Or maybe she did. Nobody know for sure. But she never come back.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
The silence between us changes shape. It's not comfortable anymore.
My father took someone from {$catName}'s world. Someone they trusted. Someone who mattered.
I stare at the screen and try to make the pieces fit. My father, the quiet man with the compass, the man who read me bedtime stories, walked into a world that welcomed him and tore a piece of it away.
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: My people were... hurt. They trusted him. They open doors for him that they not open for outsiders. And he take one of their own and disappear.
{$catName}: That is all I know. The elders not like to say more. It is... old wound.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    -> ...That was my father.
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: ...I know. I think I know since you first tell me about your family.
        {$catName}: I am sorry. I not know how to say sooner.
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    -> (say nothing)
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: ...You are quiet. I think maybe you understand who I talk about.
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The words sit in my chest like stones. My father lived on an alien planet. He earned their trust, and then he betrayed it.
<<set $negSelfPerception += 2>>
I feel something crack open inside me. The man I grew up admiring... who taught me patience, who gave me my love of the stars... did something unforgivable.
And the person I've been building something with is the one who paid for it.
    -> ...I need to go.
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: I understand. I... I am sorry.
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    -> I can't do this right now.
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: ...Okay.
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
I close the channel. The screen goes dark.
<<jump AfterCatLeavesDay3>>
===

title: AfterCatLeavesDay3
position: 915,224
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
The screen collapses to static. Then nothing.
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I sit there, staring at the monitor, hands flat on the console. My reflection stares back, and for the first time, I look at it like a stranger.
The report template is still open. The cursor blinks.
I can't do it. Not tonight.
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
I push back from the desk. The chair scrapes against the floor, too loud in the silence.
The report can wait. Everything can wait.
<<if $negSelfPerception >= $posSelfPerception + 3>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 2>>
    It hits all at once.
    My father was a thief. Not of things, but of trust. He walked into a world that welcomed him, earned their love, and ripped someone away from it.
    {$catName}'s people lost someone because of him. Because of my family. And that loss became the fear that shaped everything — the rules, the silence, the walls {$catName} grew up inside.
    And here I am, floating through the same void, pretending I'm a good person.
    I feel like I was built on a rotten foundation.
<<elseif $negSelfPerception > $posSelfPerception>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
    The thought spirals: how do I look {$catName} in the eye after this?
    My father took someone from their world. Someone who mattered. And that betrayal is the reason {$catName}'s people fear humans, the reason talking to me is dangerous for them.
    I think about every kind thing {$catName} said to me. Every moment of patience.
    They chose to trust me despite what my father did. And I didn't even know there was something to forgive. The thought makes me feel sick.
<<else>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
    I sit with it. The weight is enormous, but I try to breathe around it.
    My father did something terrible. He took someone from {$catName}'s world, from their people, and never looked back.
    It doesn't make me him. I know that. But it rearranges everything. The man I thought I knew, the family I thought I understood.
    I'm shaken. Deeply. But I'm also still here. That has to count for something.
    I'll deal with this. Just... not tonight.
<<endif>>
<<jump EndDay3>>
===

title: EndDay3
position: 918,14
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
I don't bother turning the monitor off properly. I just let it go dark on its own.
The report sits unfinished. HQ will get a blank day from me. They can add it to the long list of things I'm failing at.
I climb into the cryopod without ceremony. No routine, no checklist, no pretending I'm fine.
Just the hum of the pod, the cold settling in, and the last image behind my eyelids. A brass compass with a sparrow on the lid, and a question I can never ask my father.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 3>>
<<jump DreamDay3>>
===

title: DreamDay3
position: 915,500
---
<<stop_music>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show BlackHole1>>
The dream starts at the viewport.
The star is there, brighter than it should be, filling the glass like a searchlight. And at its center, the dark spot. The hole that swallowed six expeditions and my father with them.
In the dream, I'm closer than I should be. Much closer. The ship is moving faster than physics should allow, drawn forward as if the dark spot is breathing me in.
I try to check the instruments but they're blank. Every screen, every readout, just black glass reflecting my face back at me.
<<show BlackHole2>>
The dark spot grows. It stops looking like a blemish on a star and starts looking like a mouth. The light around it bends, stretches, thins into threads that spiral inward and vanish.
A black hole. It was always a black hole.
The ship groans. The hull flexes. I feel the pull in my chest, not pain exactly, but a certainty. A direction I can't refuse.
<<show BlackHole3>>
The stars outside begin to streak, then smear, then disappear entirely. The viewport fills with nothing. Pure, total nothing.
    -> (reach toward it)
        I don't fight it. My hand lifts toward the glass, and the darkness reaches back.
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            And just before the black swallows everything, I feel something I didn't expect: peace. Not the empty kind. The kind that comes from finally letting go of the need to steer.
            Maybe the dark spot isn't an ending. Maybe it's just a door I haven't learned to see through yet.
        <<else>>
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            The darkness takes me without resistance. I was always heading here. Every choice, every report, every sleepless night was just a longer route to the same inevitable point.
            I wonder if my father felt this too, right at the end. The quiet relief of not having to pretend anymore.
        <<endif>>
    -> (close your eyes)
        I shut my eyes before the nothing can reach them. As if that changes anything.
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            Behind my eyelids, I see light. Not the star. Something warmer, softer. The afterimage of every small thing that kept me going: push-ups in a tin can, a puzzle with an alien, a sky I was shown for two seconds.
            The black hole can have the ship. It can't have that.
        <<else>>
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            Behind my eyelids, there's the same darkness. No escape, no difference. Open or closed, the result is the same.
            I've been falling into this my whole life. The mission just gave it a name.
        <<endif>>
<<show BlackHole4>>
My vision goes black. The hum of the ship, the groan of the hull, the pull in my chest, all of it collapses into silence.
For a long time, there is nothing at all.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 2>>
<<jump StartDay4>>
===
